#
# Flash Circular Buffer
#

config FCB
	bool "Flash Circular Buffer support"
	depends on FLASH_MAP
	select CRC
	depends on FLASH_PAGE_LAYOUT
	help
	  Enable support of Flash Circular Buffer.

if FCB

config FCB_ALLOW_FIXED_ENDMARKER
	bool "Allow FCB instances to have a fixed endmarker"
	help
	  This allows the FCB instances to disable CRC checks in
	  favor of increased write throughput.

config FCB_ENDMARKER_NEVER_ERASED
	bool "Never use the erased value as an entry's end marker"
	help
	  The end marker of an entry is the CRC-8 of its length and data, written
	  after the data. When that CRC-8 equals the erased value of the flash,
	  a finished entry cannot be told from one whose write was cut short by
	  a power loss before its end marker was written: both read back as
	  valid, and the cut-short one hands half-written data to the reader.
	  With this option such a CRC-8 is written as its complement instead, so
	  an end marker that is still erased never validates an entry.

	  Entries written without this option whose CRC-8 is the erased value
	  (one in 256) read as invalid with it, so turn it on before data is
	  first written, or accept losing those entries once.

endif
